  "id": "common-trait",
  "term": "common trait",
  "definition": "In this historical usage, a common trait is the shared feature that unites different methods under one general label. Here it refers to what all introspective methods have in common: they are forms of scientific observation aimed at describing conscious experience rather than explaining its causes.",
